		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 199.644 69.342 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3 3)
				(thickness 1)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "c847596d-35d4-4bf6-811a-ec9295e6f351")
	)
	(text "DIGITAL & ANALOG SENSORS SUBSYSTEM DESIGN NOTES (SENSORS BLOCK)\n=======================================================================================\nProject: OpenMycoNet COMBO_NODE Rev 3.6\nStatus: FINAL PRODUCTION RELEASE\n\n1. BIOELECTRIC & IMPEDANCE FRONT-END (ELECTRODES & EC STIMULATION)\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• INA333 INSTRUMENTATION AMPLIFIER (U10):\n  - Measures microvolt-level bioelectric potential differences between INA+ and INA- inputs.\n  - ESD and transient protection provided by inline 10 kΩ series resistors (R56, R57) and\n    low-capacitance ESD clamp array (D3).\n  - Pin 5 (REF) tied directly to active VMID_REFF (1.65 V) to center output swing at mid-rail.\n\n• 1.65 V MIDPOINT REFERENCE BUFFER & DISTRIBUTION (U19 / VMID_REFF):\n  - Midpoint Divider: R43/R44 standardized to 100 kΩ filtered by C34 (100 nF) to GND,\n    providing a stable 1.65 V midpoint with minimal current draw (16.5 µA).\n  - Standalone Voltage Follower: Actively buffered by dedicated low-quiescent op-amp\n    U19 (OPA333AIDBVR, SOT-23-5) with Pin 3 (+IN) tied to C34, and Pin 4 (-IN) shorted to\n    Pin 1 (OUT) in a 1:1 unity-gain configuration.\n  - Active Output: Pin 1 drives net VMID_REFF through R62 (22 Ω isolation resistor) with\n    dedicated local decoupling C51 (100 nF to GND).\n  - Star Reference Distribution: VMID_REFF provides clean 1.65 V virtual ground to:\n    1) INA333 (U10) Pin 5 (REF) for mid-rail bi-directional output swing.\n    2) Input bias offset network R32.\n    3) High-value 10 MΩ bias return resistors R63 and R64.\n    4) EC stimulation return path (J11 Pin 2 & bottom of R46).\n\n• OPA2320 TRANSIMPEDANCE / EC RECEIVER (U13):\n  - Channel A (U13A): Functions as high-gain transimpedance stage for bio-impedance signals.\n  - Channel B (U13B): Serves strictly as the EC probe receive amplifier. Pin 7 (+INB) \n    connects to 1.65 V midpoint, and Pin 9 (VOUT_B) feeds back to Pin 8 (INB-) through \n    parallel network R40||R41 = 1.65 kΩ and C30 = 10 pF. Completely isolated from R62/VMID_REFF\n    to prevent soil signal crosstalk during active EC stimulation.\n  - Shutdown Control: ANA_SHUT line from MCU GPIO42 controls active/sleep modes (< 1 µA sleep).\n\n• TS5A3159 ANALOG SWITCH & ATTENUATOR (U15):\n  - Provides gain-switching and AC excitation path selection for EC probe measurements.\n  - Driven by EC_ENABLE via MCU GPIO48 (pulled LOW by R26 to disable stimulus at boot).\n\n2. DIGITAL SENSOR ARRAY & ANALOG CONVERSION\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• ADS1115 16-BIT PRECISION ADC (U14):\n  - Digitizes low-frequency analog sensor outputs over shared I2C bus (SDA/SCL).\n  - Powered via continuous +3.3VA rail for noise-free conversion baseline.\n\n• SCD41 NDIR CO2 SENSOR (U11):\n  - Measures ambient CO2, temperature, and relative humidity over shared I2C bus.\n  - Software low-power commands utilized to enter low-power single-shot measurement mode.\n\n• DS3231MZ HIGH-PRECISION RTC (U12):\n  - Provides precise timestamping; backed up by CR1216 coin cell (BT1) on VBATT rail.\n  - Communicates via I2C with dedicated interrupt pin connected to MCU.\n\n• DS18B20 1-WIRE DIGITAL TEMPERATURE PROBE (J8):\n  - Dedicated 1-Wire interface with 4.7 kΩ pull-up resistor (R61) to +3.3V.\n\n3. POWER-GATED SENSORS & ILLUMINATION PROBES\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• TPS22919 LOAD SWITCH (U18 - MOISTURE SENSOR POWER GATE):\n  - Controls power to capacitive soil moisture probe (J9) via MOISTURE_SLEEP (GPIO41).\n  - Completely isolates moisture sensor power rail during MCU deep sleep to extend battery life.\n\n• 470 nm BLUE LIGHT ILLUMINATION PROBES (J5 / J6 - LED BANK):\n  - Pin 1 (Power): Connected directly to +BATT supply through dedicated 68 Ω series\n    resistors (R59, R60, 0805, 1/8 W). Forward current fixed at ~16.2 mA @ 4.2 V BATT\n    (VF ≈ 3.1 V), preventing voltage sags on the primary +3.3V digital supply.\n  - Pin 2 (Control): Connected to Drain of low-side BSS138 N-channel MOSFETs (Q1, Q2),\n    driven in active-HIGH logic via LED_PWM1 (GPIO11) and LED_PWM2 (GPIO10) with\n    10 kΩ gate pull-downs (R34, R37) to ensure zero emission during MCU boot.\n\n4. SUBSYSTEM INTERCONNECT MATRIX\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCOMPONENT / CONNECTOR  | SIGNAL / NET NAME   | INTERFACE TYPE | POWER RAIL / CONTROL\n-----------------------+---------------------+----------------+------------------------\nU10 (INA333)           | INA+ / INA-         | Analog Diff    | +3.3VA / R56/57+D3 Prot.\nU13 (OPA2320S)         | ANA_SHUT            | Digital GPIO42 | +3.3VA (Sleep < 1 µA)\nU19 (LPV811DBV)        | VMID_REFF           | Analog Ref     | +3.3VA / Standby 425 nA\nU15 (TS5A3159)         | EC_ENABLE           | Digital GPIO48 | +3.3VA (Pulled LOW R26)\nEC PROBE DRIVER        | DAC_OUT             | 16 Hz AC Stim  | +3.3VA / C28 (100 µF)\nU14 (ADS1115)          | I2C_BUS (SDA/SCL)   | Shared I2C     | +3.3VA (Continuous)\nU11 (SCD41)            | I2C_BUS (SDA/SCL)   | Shared I2C     | Soft-Sleep Command\nDS3231MZ (RTC)         | RTC_IN              | I2C / INT      | +3.3V / CR1216 Backup\nJ8 (DS18B20)           | DS18B20_DATA        | 1-Wire         | +3.3V (4.7 kΩ R61 Pull-up)\nU18 / J9 (Moisture)    | MOISTURE_SLEEP      | Power Gated    | TPS22919 via GPIO41\nQ1/Q2 / J5/J6 (LEDs)   | LED_PWM1 / PWM2     | Low-Side PWM   | +BATT Rail (R59/R60 68 Ω)\n======================================================================================="
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 13.716 103.378 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "d54cd75e-e7cc-4c45-8e10-3ad5fd343ef0")
	)
